 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Bernie's hockey puck bounced higher than the scoreboard. Twice.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 2.946
  },
  {
   "text": "It was the championship final, and the puck had landed in the nachos.",
   "s": 3.146,
   "e": 6.351
  },
  {
   "text": "It started with one complaint: \"Your pucks are too cold to touch!\"",
   "s": 6.551,
   "e": 9.59
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Nice and toasty!\" said Bernie, and baked every puck in the pizza oven.",
   "s": 9.71,
   "e": 13.016
  },
  {
   "text": "First face-off: the puck hit the ice, went boing, and bounced off the ref's helmet.",
   "s": 13.216,
   "e": 16.639
  },
  {
   "text": "Then Waffles, the bear goalie, complained it was too chilly to nap.",
   "s": 16.839,
   "e": 19.96
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Nice and toasty!\" said Bernie, and cranked every heater to max.",
   "s": 20.16,
   "e": 23.177
  },
  {
   "text": "Now each slapshot was pinball: forty-one bounces, one goal, wrong net.",
   "s": 23.377,
   "e": 27.034
  },
  {
   "text": "But why would a cold puck stay down, while a warm one flies?",
   "s": 27.234,
   "e": 29.732
  },
  {
   "text": "A puck is rubber. Warm rubber is springy, like a bouncy ball.",
   "s": 30.032,
   "e": 32.976
  },
  {
   "text": "Freeze it, and the rubber goes stiff: it slides flat instead of jumping.",
   "s": 33.376,
   "e": 36.735
  },
  {
   "text": "So real rinks keep their pucks in a freezer until game time.",
   "s": 36.935,
   "e": 39.79
  },
  {
   "text": "Bernie froze the pucks. Waffles moved into the freezer. Nice and toasty.",
   "s": 39.99,
   "e": 43.713
  }
 ],
